<Base title="Getting started with Saydraft — Offline dictation setup" description="Set up local speech models, choose your microphone, try a first dictation, and learn Saydraft’s Windows shortcuts.">
  <main id="main" class="document container"><p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p><h1>Your first<br /><em>few words.</em></h1>
    <h2>1. Get the app</h2><p>Start with the current instructions on the <a href={`${base}download/`}>download and setup page</a>. Saydraft runs on Windows 10 and 11.</p>
    <h2>2. Choose your microphone</h2><p>In setup’s Microphone page, keep Default Windows input or choose Refresh inputs to find a named device. Test input runs a ten-second, level-only check without transcription or saved audio. If needed, use the microphone-privacy link to allow desktop apps in Windows settings. Start in a quiet room and speak at a comfortable volume.</p>
    <h2>3. Set up your local models</h2><p>On Set up models, Check this PC offers a provisional capability recommendation. Use speech recommendation selects the suggested speech model; it does not run a performance benchmark, enable AI cleanup, or download anything.</p><p>Review the model’s download size and licenses, then choose Download / Resume. Setup shows overall progress and each file’s transfer/checksum phases, with Pause available. Installed files are checked in the background, including pinned dependencies. Later launches reuse installed models.</p><p>After installation, choose Check model performance to measure the selected speech model with bundled audio. Preparation is separate from three timed speech samples. This opens no microphone, downloads nothing, and leaves unavailable AI cleanup speed unmeasured. Stop check waits for native work to finish; successful reports stay separate from setup preference saving.</p><p>For Bengali or Arabic, add the optional shared All languages model. One download serves both languages; choosing a language starts no transfer.</p><p>Next becomes available when the selected speech model is ready. Catalog packages must pass their file checks. If you already have a local Whisper model, Check model performance can confirm that it loads offline. Finish checks the current model files again before saving your choices. Cancel, hiding setup, or going Back cancels a pending Finish. Permission diagnostics and fresh-profile manual acceptance remain in progress. See the <a href="https://github.com/tanzir71/saydraft/blob/main/docs/ONBOARDING.md">first-run implementation guide</a> for current behavior and remaining work.</p>
    <h2>4. Choose a shortcut and practice</h2><p>Setup’s Shortcut page keeps existing custom bindings or shows the Wispr-compatible preset for a fresh profile. Choose Learn shortcut, then press and release your keys while setup stays focused. Learning lasts up to ten seconds; Escape cancels. You can also enter a shortcut manually and check for conflicts.</p><p>Continue to Try it, with chat and email fields inside setup. Preparing an installed speech model opens no microphone. Hold your shortcut or choose Record, speak a short example, then release or choose Stop and preview. Each practice recording is limited to one minute. Review the raw words, cleaned text, and edit chips. Practice audio stays in memory and creates no History entry; it uses no external paste or clipboard. Escape cancels a recording. You can continue without recording.</p><p>If an app stop or Settings change ends practice, choose Prepare practice explicitly when you are ready. If setup cannot confirm that practice stopped, cancel setup and restart Saydraft as prompted.</p><p>The defaults are <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Win</kbd> to dictate and F9 as the alternate. Ctrl + Win + Space toggles hands-free. Existing custom bindings are preserved.</p>
    <h2>5. Make it sound like you</h2><p>In Style quick pick, choose Casual or Formal for Messages and Email. The rules preview uses your last practice transcript or a labeled example. Finish saves changed choices and opens Home after practice stops; your current cleanup intensity and AI settings stay unchanged. Cancel preserves saved preferences, while downloaded files remain separate.</p><p>Later, adjust every app group in Hub → Style, add names to Dictionary, and turn frequently used text into Snippets. AI cleanup is optional; rules-only cleanup works without a text model.</p>
    <h2>6. Try it offline</h2><p>With a compatible speech model installed, open an ordinary text editor and put the cursor in an editable field. Hold your shortcut, speak, then release. Disconnect Wi-Fi and try another sentence. Speech and cleanup run on your PC. Shift + Alt + Z pastes the last saved transcript during daily use. See <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>privacy and offline verification</a> for the boundaries.</p>
    <h2>If something feels wrong</h2><p>Check that the selected model is installed and the microphone meter responds. Use an ordinary, non-elevated text editor for the first test. Password and protected fields are excluded. Keep your transcript in History if an app cannot accept insertion.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/tanzir71/saydraft/issues">Report a problem on GitHub ↗</a>. Avoid including private transcripts or audio in public reports.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
